`verilator_config
// hdl-lint waivers (modules/synthframe/bin/hdl-lint, `verilator --lint-only -Wall` on the MiSTer
// top). Each waiver names a rule and a file; all but the style rules (DECLFILENAME, BLKSEQ,
// PINCONNECTEMPTY, GENUNNAMED, TIMESCALEMOD, PROCASSINIT, UNUSEDPARAM) also name the message.
// `hdl-lint --update CORE` appends waivers for new warnings; review them before committing.
// Reviewed 2026-11-26: no waiver hides a functional bug. Notes on the non-style ones:
// fx68k (mister/rtl/fx68k, Jorge Cwik's 68000, vendored): Irdecod/Nanod are written from more
// than one process, which Verilator flags (MULTIDRIVEN, BLKANDNBLK, UNOPTFLAT, ALWCOMBORDER);
// Quartus and every fx68k core build it as is.
// proteus_snd.sv: vout <= mul2 >>> 16 keeps the 17 bits the model keeps; pl/pr are signed and
// sign-extend into acc_l/acc_r. proteus_sys.sv: snd_voice takes 5 of the pan-voice subtraction.
// panel.sv: PULSE/GAP/DELAY/REPEAT are CLK_HZ divisions (at most 26.7 M at 80 MHz) into a 25-bit
// counter. init_macro.sv: tick (17 bits) against MS = CLK_HZ / 1000 (80 000).
// p2k_fx.sv: sa[sx - 2] runs only for sx 2..5; the 8-bit init_a/DIV constants and 3-bit
// indices into 12/16-entry arrays extend. Proteus.sv: VIDEO_ARX/ARY (Template_MiSTer).

lint_off -rule UNUSEDPARAM -file "*p2k/rtl/cpu/mcf5206e_periph.sv"
lint_off -rule UNUSEDSIGNAL -file "*p2k/rtl/cpu/mcf5206e_periph.sv" -match "Bits of function variable are not used: 'd'[7]"
lint_off -rule UNUSEDSIGNAL -file "*p2k/rtl/cpu/mcf5206e_periph.sv" -match "Bits of function variable are not used: 'u'[164:117,100:0]"
